{"summary":"Complete ledger built from input/disclosure.md plus the USER passages of input/conversation.md; brief.md used only for title, applicant/inventor, priority and government-support formalities. Every limitation of claims 1-20, every one of the 17 numbered parts, and every specific structure, relationship, result, material, position, connection, operating condition and variant in the Field, Summary, Detailed Description, Abstract and the six figure briefs traces to an exact affirmative source passage. Key traces: rigid base with first/second sides, motor and air-extraction mechanism (vacuum pump) on the first side, chamber on the second side, rigid low-friction loop/skirt of plastic, metal, PTFE or a combination at the perimeter of the second side (disclosure para. 11); the perimeter is not an airtight seal, restricts but does not stop inflow, air enters beneath it, continuous extraction keeps the chamber below atmosphere, and the differential holds the device down without operator pressure (para. 13); rigid-path transfer with substantially less damping than a flexible cup, and free sliding to successive areas while the vacuum maintains contact (paras. 7, 15); guiding handles and a rope/wire/cable pulling element giving decoupled control (para. 17); stirring elements through which the vibration produces constant forward motion with no pulling and no hand guidance (conversation.md line 223, USER). Claim 1/11/15 element-by-element, and dependent claims 2-10, 12-14 and 16-20, are each covered; nothing optional or dependent is untraced. Background prior-art characterizations with [REF:...] keys were treated as out of scope for this pass.

Functional-surface-geometry pass: no brief states a taper, angle, runout direction, relative depth, deeper end, radial or circumferential end position of a functional face, or any contact topology beyond what the text supports. FIG. 4 draws the bearing face as a plain closing line and the clearance as open unhatched space "shown enlarged for clarity", matching the description; FIG. 2 shows the loop bearing on the covering element and FIG. 4 a place where the clearance is present, which is exactly the source condition that the perimeter maintains rigid contact while admitting air beneath it, rendered in the text as "along at least part of the perimeter member". Depiction conventions considered and cleared because they are confined to the figure briefs, expressly marked schematic, and add no technical function while the claims, description and Brief Description of the Drawings stay shape-neutral: the rectangular slab, ring and band forms; the schematic band and leg depths; the generic motor, pump and handle blocks and their order on the top face ("no particular handle form, size or mounting arrangement being asserted"); the two stirring blocks with number, form and drawn position marked as a convention and no engagement with the covering element asserted; the pulling element's meeting place "shown schematically with no attachment formation". FIG. 2 splits the fluid-communication broken lines so no passage through the base is asserted, and FIG. 3 keeps the second side plain, both consistent with the earlier removal of the through-base duct. No application-text sentence adds or broadens an embodiment to justify a renderer's choice: the drawings section uses only "shown schematically" and "omitted for clarity", with no "by way of example" or "any closed outline" wording.

Text-consistency pass: section lines carry the same repeated designations 2-2 and 4-4 in the FIG. 3 source-view brief, in the FIG. 2 and FIG. 4 resulting-view briefs, in the Brief Description of the Drawings, and in the detailed description. The FIG. 2 entry in the Brief Description now enumerates the same cut bodies as the FIG. 2 brief, with the air-extraction mechanism in elevation and the motor and handle omitted. All 17 numerals are defined once, each is used in the detailed description, each appears on at least one sheet, and every numeral named in a brief is in the table; numeral 10 means the whole machine, 12 the base and 24 the perimeter member consistently across FIG. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6. Claim and description wording match term for term ("bearing face that is an end face", "clearance remaining, along at least part of the perimeter member", "vibration transmission path", "while the pressure differential is maintained"), embodiment numbering matches between the drawings section and the description, all six figures are referenced in the description, antecedent basis is sound in all three independent claims, and the claim set is 20 claims with 3 independents. No drafting note, placeholder, open question, instruction to a person, unresolved alternative or internal comment remains in any draft section, the numeral table, or any figure brief; the only bracketed text in the draft is valid [REF:...] citation keys. The full ledger is supported and the proposed text is internally consistent.","findings":[]}
